  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "A Record Keeping System, in the blockchain domain, is an immutable, append-only ledger in which transactions or state changes are cryptographically hashed, linked via Merkle trees, and validated by a consensus mechanism to provide a tamper-evident audit trail. It replaces or augments traditional centralised databases in applications requiring transparent provenance, non-repudiation, and multi-party data integrity\u2014including asset registries, supply-chain tracking, and compliance logging.",
